    "Scouting Notes": "Reliever\n Curveball is a nasty pitch, late breaking, sharp, lots of movement. Everything you're looking for in a breaking ball.\n Fastball is low 90's still with some late life on it though\n Changeup is a solid pitch as well, was once thought to be his best, breaking ball definitely is now\n Command is better than I expected after his ACL walk numbers\n Very intriguing arm",
    "Notes Updated 2": "7/13/2023",
    "Scouting Notes 2": "DRAFT REPORT\nAnother high school pick was not what I was expecting in round 12, but it would be the second of seven high school selections the Brewers made on day three. Johnson has a fastball in the low 90’s that he has been able to hold deep into his outings. He also mixes in a slider and a changeup, the changeup is probably the better of the two offerings at this moment. Strong command was a theme with each of the first two picks on day three. Johnson may be another tough sign, depending on the type of bonus pool the Brewers actually have left over.",
